{"type":"text","timestamp":1791297057989,"sessionID":"ses_eee62f560ffe3fOuWTJCagfjGr","part":{"id":"prt_1119fe57c001J2dBKZ8TmiSb5P","messageID":"msg_1119fcb8b001aCz04lrxSMhPtq","sessionID":"ses_eee62f560ffe3fOuWTJCagfjGr","type":"text","text":"All 6 visible tests pass, plus extra checks against the documented edge cases. Bugs fixed:\n\n1. **`parse_date` (parse.py)** — returned `(year, day, month)`. It swapped the month and day. Now returns `(year, month, day)`.\n2. **`format_cents` (money.py)** — broke on negative values. Floor division on a negative number produced `-$-4.90` for `-310`. Now it formats `abs(cents)` and prepends the sign, so `-310` gives `-$3.10` and `-5` gives `-$0.05`.\n3. **`top_items` (report.py)** — sorted totals ascending, so it returned the smallest items. It also ignored the tie-break rule. Now sorts by total descending, then item name ascending, as the docstring specifies.","time":{"start":1791297054076,"end":1791297057984}}}
